#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - cohomcalg 0.32 raw Makefile hardcoded g++ override
# Source package: cohomcalg/0.32
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-cohomcalg-0.32-makefile-gxx-override
trigger_tool:           make
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        make: g\+\+: No such file or directory|No such file or directory

severity:               2
category:               build-system|make|toolchain
match_keywords:         Makefile, CC := g++, LD := g++, hardcoded compiler, g++ missing, clang++, OHOS CI, compiler override, make CC=, raw Makefile, no configure, GNU make, command-line variable

title:                  Raw Makefile hardcoding CC:=g++ fails on OHOS (no g++); override CC/LD on the make command line

root_cause:             >
    Some legacy Makefiles hardcode the compiler in the recipe variables, e.g.
    cohomcalg 0.32's top Makefile has `CC := g++` and `LD := g++` (plus defines
    `DEFS := -DPOLYLIB_BITS=64`). The OHOS PC toolchain ships clang/clang++
    only — there is no g++ — so `make` fails immediately:
        make: g++: No such file or directory
    The project is a raw Makefile build (no configure/CMake), so the standard
    autotools workaround (export CXX=clang++ before configure) does not apply;
    the compiler must be overridden directly on the make command line:
        make -j1 CC=clang++ LD=clang++
    GNU make command-line variable assignments override the file's `:=` defaults.
    -j1 is required anyway on HMDFS/SELinux workers (make jobserver mkfifo is
    denied; see forbid below).

affected_scope:         Any raw-Makefile (no configure/CMake) C/C++ project whose Makefile
                        hardcodes CC/LD to g++, adapted to OHOS (clang-only toolchain).

verification_cmd:       |
  cd <worktree> && make clean && make -j1 CC=clang++ LD=clang++ && ls -l bin/cohomcalg

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           make-cmdline-cc-override
rec_description: >
    In build() (or the manual build command), pass `CC=clang++ LD=clang++` on the make
    command line. Inside a Conan recipe resolve the compiler from
    tools.build:compiler_executables (R33) — never from bare ${CXX} — then
    `self.run(f'make -j1 CC="{cc}" LD="{cc}"', cwd=self.source_folder)`.
    Keep DEFS/POLYLIB_BITS as the Makefile already defines it.
rec_command:            |
  make -j1 CC=clang++ LD=clang++
rec_auto_fix:           true
rec_impl:               manual

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      patch-makefile-cc
fallback_description:   If the picky packaging requires no command-line override, patch the Makefile
                        `CC := g++` -> `CC ?= clang++` (or inject via a portability patch).
fallback_command:       sed -i 's/^CC *:= *g++/CC ?= clang++/; s/^LD *:= *g++/LD ?= clang++/' Makefile
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          patch

forbid_1_pattern:       make -j$(nproc)|-j[0-9]+ on HMDFS
forbid_1_reason:        GNU make jobserver uses mkfifo; HMDFS/SELinux denies it (E074-class) -> jobserver error or hang.
forbid_1_consequence:   `make: jobserver mkfifo: Operation not permitted`; build never progresses.
forbid_2_pattern:       export CC=clang export CXX=clang++ (for a raw Makefile with no configure)
forbid_2_reason:        The Makefile uses `CC := g++` (:= overrides environment); env vars are ignored for these assignments.
forbid_2_consequence:   Compiler stays g++, build fails with the same "g++ not found" error.

similar_to:             [E053]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

